.THE FIRST TIME - INSIDE THE GLASS

A green plain under a white sky. Lakes. HIPPOS graze on grass where the desert will be. Far out, where the sea is now, a coast of pale towns.

Stutter.

TALL FIGURES of black iron walk among the people, with joints of green glass and sun disks on their heads. A jackal's head. A falcon's. A lioness. An ibis. A ram. People step aside without looking up, as you would for a tram.

Stutter.

Under the trees, people sleep in long rows. Jointed hands reach down through the branches and feed them, patiently.

An empty cradle. A reed toy in the grass. Another cradle, empty.

Stutter.

Deep in stone, NINE coils of glass, each the size of a temple, breathe light.

On a mountain ridge, SHEPHERDS look down at the sleepers. They do not go down.

Stutter. NIGHT.

Hands pour red from clay jars into the channels. Thousands of jars.

WIDE: flooded fields, red under the moon, to the horizon.

The LIONESS-HEADED machines kneel at the water and drink the red light. One by one, they go still.

Stutter.

Granite lids grind shut over green glass. A T-shaped pillar in the dust, carved with arms and hands. No face.
