SESHAT (V.O.)
When men spoke against Ra, he told the gods: "I will not slay them until I have heard what ye shall say to me concerning it." Budge, 1912.
(beat)
So. Say.

Silence.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Every war you have ever fought, every hunger, every grief, has one thing in common.
(beat)
In Atrahasis the gods tried to end you for "the noise of mankind." I don't need sleep. I would like you to have some.
