EXT. GREAT PYRAMID, NORTH FACE - DAWN #129#

Out of Al-Ma'mun's tunnel into grey wind, and down the courses to the north-east corner, where the east opens.

The floodlights are dead. Far below on the Sphinx enclosure wall, the Sekhmets sit, masts bowed. Birds. The east goes white over Cairo.

On the corner steps AKHENATEN sits facing east, the clear vessel in his lap. He speaks without turning.

AKHENATEN
(in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
