INT. GEM, TUTANKHAMUN GALLERIES - DAY #134#

White-gloved human hands set the scarab pectoral back on its mount; the green glass takes the light. The bronze trumpet is laid on its cushion.

INT. KV62, ANTECHAMBER - SUNSET #135#

The mummy lies in its climate case on its tray of sand, in new linen, face under a linen shroud. Only the gold wrist seam shows. Fresh cornflowers on the glass. Beyond, the north wall conserved, the painted EYE restored.

By the door, a typed roster: one name for every sunset (COMP). Hers is first. Nour sits alone, Rami's notebook on her knee. In the corner, a small security SPEAKER.

The last sun leaves the valley.

NOUR
(in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
